 namespace WTF {
 
+// Process-local overrides of every AutomaticThread's idle behavior, for an embedder that forks a process and then
+// denies it thread creation and signals. Until one is set, every AutomaticThread behaves as upstream.
+//
+// setColloAutomaticThreadTimeout replaces each thread's idle timeout. A short one lets parked threads retire so the
+// process can become single-threaded before it forks; one longer than the process's life pins them, because a
+// thread that retires after thread creation is denied can never be started again.
+//
+// setColloAutomaticThreadCacheRelease makes a thread that has waited that long without work release its malloc
+// thread cache once, through releaseFastMallocFreeMemoryForThisThread, and keep waiting. A pinned thread never
+// retires, which is what would otherwise free its cache, and libpas can stop another thread's allocators only by
+// suspending that thread with a signal. While the cache stays active the libpas scavenger keeps polling for it and
+// never reaches its deep sleep. The release has no effect when it is not shorter than the effective timeout, since
+// the thread then retires first.
+//
+// Changing either value wakes every registered thread that is parked, and each one measures the time it has already
+// waited against the new values. clearColloAutomaticThreadOverrides removes both.
+WTF_EXPORT_PRIVATE void setColloAutomaticThreadTimeout(Seconds);
+WTF_EXPORT_PRIVATE void setColloAutomaticThreadCacheRelease(Seconds idleTime);
+WTF_EXPORT_PRIVATE void clearColloAutomaticThreadOverrides();
+// A forked child inherits the registry's entries but none of the threads behind them; this forgets the entries.
+// An override change no longer wakes a thread whose AutomaticThread object predates the reset, so a child sets its
+// overrides before it starts those threads again.
+WTF_EXPORT_PRIVATE void colloResetAutomaticThreadRegistry();
+
